        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பகை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பகை — pakai — \"enmity; a feud\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "இரண்டு குடும்பங்களுக்கும் இடையில் பல வருடமாகப் பகை. iraṇṭu kuṭumpaṅkaḷukkum iṭaiyil pala varuṭamākap pakai. There has been a feud between the two families for many years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பகைவன், an enemy, in written Tamil."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பகை (pakai) is native Dravidian (DEDR 3808), in the family of பகு paku, \"to be split, to be at variance\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
